From: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:19:07 +0000
Subject: PCI: sky1-cix: fix AER interrupt storms

On an Orange Pi 6 the NVMe root port's non-fatal AER line (aer_nf)
sometimes fires nonstop right after link training, with every AER
status register clear. The handler returned IRQ_HANDLED and logged two
lines per interrupt to the console with the AER lock held, which ended
in a hard lockup (7.x) or a silent reset under load (6.18).

The cause: local error register 0 bit 31, the LTSSM-transition
indication, latches unmasked on that line and nothing acks it, so the
level interrupt never drops.

- Ack the LTSSM-transition indication on the AER lines the way the
  local IRQ handler does (AXI slave indication bit, LTSSM status
  channels, then the latched bit), and treat it as handled.
- Clear latched local errors that are masked from the local interrupt
  but still latch.
- Guard against any other cause: read root, correctable and
  uncorrectable status and DEVSTA first; if none shows an error, return
  IRQ_NONE (rate-limited warning). Each AER line keeps its own count:
  after a burst of 64 such interrupts on a line (a gap of more than 1 s
  resets it), disable that line, dump the registers once, and re-enable
  it 2 s later, up to 5 times per line.
- On remove and in sky1_pcie_disable_irq(), disable the AER lines
  first (waiting for running handlers), then cancel the pending
  re-enables, so none can run afterwards.
- Rate-limit the remaining AER logging and print it after dropping the
  lock; the per-interrupt dev_sts prints become dev_dbg.
- Log the local/AER IRQ numbers at probe.

Developed and tested on the Sky1-Linux copy of this driver, whose AER
code is the same as here apart from register-base and helper names. On an
Orange Pi 6 (ACPI boot) on 7.3.5 the condition was hit at boot
("aer_nf: LTSSM transition indication latched ... cleared" four times)
and the storm never started. The guard and the latched-error clear alone,
on 6.18.64, took the board from silent resets under build load to an hour
of build + stress load with none. This port builds against v7.3.6 with
config-7.3.defconfig.

Signed-off-by: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
